@startuml Decorator-Stream-Problem
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title BEFORE — extending a Stream by subclassing (the problem)

abstract class Stream {
  + putInt(value : int) : void
  + putString(value : String) : void
  + close() : void
  # {abstract} handleBufferFull() : void
  # takeBuffer() : String
}

class FileStream {
  # handleBufferFull() : void
  # store(block : String) : void
}

class SocketStream {
  # handleBufferFull() : void
  # store(packet : String) : void
}

class CompressingFileStream {
  # handleBufferFull() : void
}

class ASCII7FileStream {
  # handleBufferFull() : void
}

class CompressingASCII7FileStream {
  # handleBufferFull() : void
}

class CompressingSocketStream {
  # handleBufferFull() : void
}

Stream <|-- FileStream
Stream <|-- SocketStream
FileStream <|-- CompressingFileStream
FileStream <|-- ASCII7FileStream
CompressingFileStream <|-- CompressingASCII7FileStream
SocketStream <|-- CompressingSocketStream

note right of CompressingSocketStream
  Body identical, character for
  character, to CompressingFileStream.
  Only the superclass differs.
end note

note bottom of CompressingASCII7FileStream
  Inherits from CompressingFileStream
  but reuses nothing: the parent applies
  half the pipeline and there is no way
  to insert a step, so both transformations
  are written out again.
end note

note as N1
  **Two axes multiply.**
  transformations x destinations = classes.
  2 x 2 destinations is already six classes here,
  and eight for full coverage. Add a third
  destination and every transformation is written
  a third time.

  **The order is in the class name**, so the other
  order is another class again.
end note

@enduml
